  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures the final show of the 2022 European tour, performed on Friday, 18 November 2022, at Vicar Street in Dublin, Ireland [1][2]. The setlist includes eighteen songs, beginning with \"Make You Suffer\" and concluding with \"No Children\" [1]. The performance is noted as being shorter than usual due to a strict curfew, a constraint that John apologized for to the audience [1]. Despite the time limit, the show is described as a fairly frenetic performance, energized by an excited Irish crowd whose cheering and clapping occasionally overwhelmed the microphones [1]. The audience’s enthusiasm was particularly strong for songs with themes related to the church [1]. The set features several rarer tracks in John’s section, including \"Bones Don't Rust\" and \"Transjordanian Blues,\" each of which has only twelve archived performances [1][2]. A standout moment is the inclusion of \"Alpha Gelida,\" which is the only performance of that song from 2022 and marks its first appearance in fifty-two archived shows, a gap of 1,001 days [1][2]. The recording is the only one available for this date, documenting the full lineage of the event [1]. It is show 356 of 467 in the archive's collection for this performer, following a previous show on 14 November 2022 at De Roma [2].",
